  "answer": "Project Zenith is a high-priority initiative aimed at driving innovation in data analytics and core operations, with a total approved budget of $2 million. The project kicked off on June 15th, led initially by Sarah Tan, with Omar Jensen guiding the development phase and recent team expansions including Mike Chen and Lisa Ray. Significant progress has been made in Phase Two, achieving a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report scheduled for November 20th. The project is currently seeking stakeholder feedback on its prototype by the end of November and is exploring partnership opportunities with TechInnovate for AI technology. Additionally, the compliance plan's budget has been increased to $55,000 to support training and audits."
